A University of Wyoming balloon sounding: a station's latest before the launch

Usage: hpr weather wyoming [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json
          Print one JSON document on standard output instead of text; errors too

      --station <STATION>
          The station's WMO number, such as 72364; not with --from, whose sounding names its own place and time

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use color. Auto colors what goes to a terminal and heeds NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE. JSON output never has color
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --time <TIME>
          The launch time in UTC; the sounding is the station's latest, at 00 or 12 UTC, before it

      --bufr
          Ask for the sounding decoded from BUFR, a row every second or two of the ascent, instead of the coded (FM 35) one

      --from <FILE>
          Read the source's answer from this file, saved earlier, instead of fetching it

      --offline
          Answer from the cache only, never the network

  -o, --output <FILE>
          Write the profile to this file, as JSON

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  Read the Reno balloon sounding launched before a launch:
      hpr weather wyoming --station 72489 --time 2026-09-26T16:00Z
  Ask for it decoded from BUFR, a row every second or two of the ascent:
      hpr weather wyoming --station 72489 --time 2026-09-26T16:00Z --bufr

Guide: https://hpr.fusionspace.co/cli.html#hpr-weather
